{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "12dcfd57-b38b-4195-b3bf-c9c9a8033c51",
      "isToggleable": false,
      "richText": [
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "Level Goal"
        }
      ],
      "type": "heading_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd517c88-5062-45b4-84e9-d49b9cfccf5f",
      "richText": [
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "The password for the next level is stored in a file called "
        },
        {
          "bold": true,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "\"--spaces in this filename--\""
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " located in the home directory."
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "id": "92e23122-a870-4217-a1ae-ab9b388612f8",
      "isToggleable": false,
      "richText": [
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "Solution"
        }
      ],
      "type": "heading_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ecea9d5-a248-4ede-a442-75736642a9d0",
      "richText": [
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "Log in using "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "ssh -p 2220 bandit2@bandit.labs.overthewire.org"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " and the password obtained in the last level. Similar to the last level, the filename in the home directory has dashes and spaces in it. Catting the filename as-is fails for two reasons: the leading dashes get read as the start of a parameter (as in "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "cat --help"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "), and the spaces split the name into what looks like several separate files (as in "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "cat file1 file2"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "). We use a relative path with the filename in quotes so the whole thing is treated as a single argument. Escaping each space ("
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "\\ "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " instead of a literal space) works the same way."
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5b35519-f8d8-4abb-a327-e4c0b5fa6f2d",
      "richText": [
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "This is the second level in a row built around filenames that fight the shell's own parsing rules. Tecmint's writeup on "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": "https://www.tecmint.com/manage-linux-filenames-with-special-characters/",
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "handling filenames with spaces and special characters"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " covers quoting and escaping options beyond the ones used here."
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
